# Programs the checker ACCEPTS and the build then refuses -- by the
# generator ("... unsupported yet") or by the C compiler.  A reader
# cannot tell such a refusal from a compiler fault, so each is owed.
# genforms.sh holds this list both ways: a name here must still pass
# `m9c --check` AND still fail to build; a fixture NOT named here must
# build and print its WANT line.  A fixed form loses its line in the
# commit that fixes it; a form found later gains a fixture and a line.
#
#   NAME                 what refuses it today (2026-10-09)
#
GfSliceOfCall        gen: SLICE() argument form -- an array a call answers (m9c.sh and lsp.sh use it as THE generator refusal)
